>
> library(mrds)
> data(book.tee.data)
> region <- book.tee.data$book.tee.region
> egdata <- book.tee.data$book.tee.dataframe
> samples <- book.tee.data$book.tee.samples
> obs <- book.tee.data$book.tee.obs
> result.io <http://result.io> <- ddf(dsmodel=~mcds(key = "hn", formula=~sex), mrmodel=~glm(~distance),
>                  data=egdata, method="io", meta.data=list(width=4))
> plot(result.io <http://result.io>, showpoints=FALSE, which=3) # pooled detection plot
> add_df_covar_line(result.io <http://result.io>$ds, data.frame(sex=c(0,1)), lty=1,col=c("red", "green"))
>
>
> Note the first argument in the call to add_df_covar_line​; I sent the ds​ element of result.io <http://result.io>​, resulting in this graph:
> You might also need to build the data.frame that you send to add_df_covar_line​ in a different way, e.g. seq(1, max(detections$GLARE))​ possibly.
>
> Let us know the outcome.
